    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (78.42) and **Austin Riley** (74.11) anchor our lineup, representing our highest efficiency plays. **James Wood** benefits from a massive park factor and an elite 0.426 xwOBA projection against Rodriguez, while his role in the leadoff spot makes him a high-floor engine for our runs category. **Austin Riley** carries a strong score driven by a significant 16% park boost and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Rogers. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.70) and **Brice Turang** (71.09) are our primary \"Strong\" plays; **Brice Turang** in particular is surging due to a plus-matchup against Sugano\u2019s 5.12 xERA, providing the necessary stability in our middle infield.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench. Despite his 42.67 score, he narrowly missed the cut because the density of high-efficiency options in the OF and MI slots forced our hand. **Vinnie Pasquantino** also presented a potential utility option, but facing a dominant arm like Skubal (2.66 xERA) rendered his efficiency profile too volatile compared to the safer, platoon-advantaged upside of **Austin Riley**. While **Jose Caballero** remains in the lineup due to his elite sprint speed and situational upside against a lefty, we are cognizant of the risks: the matchup against Luzardo is tough, and he is dragging down our overall efficiency score with a bottom-third order placement.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile conditions surrounding our bench, specifically the 42% rain risk looming over **Edwin Arroyo**. Furthermore, while **Seiya Suzuki** is active, his score of 45.41 is dangerously close to our floor, suppressed by a tough draw against Jones and a high-efficiency opposing catcher. We are rolling out a lineup built on speed-adjusted projections and park-specific advantages, but the reliance on **Jose Caballero** and **Henry Bolte** (47.93) to bolster our SB counts remains our greatest point of failure if the game scripts turn stagnant.",
